{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1154006-looking-for-a-powerful-spirit","id":1154006,"title":"Looking for a powerful spirit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-29T15:50:56-07:00","id":1154006,"title":"Looking for a powerful spirit","content":"I'm setting up a background of two warring tribes, one Fianna the other Uktena, who have been at odds since the Fianna kinfolk first settled in America. A mountain range divides the two tribes but they have fought over possession of several caerns/spiritual sites within those mountains for the last couple of centuries.<br /> <br /> Twenty odd years ago a skin dancer arose among the Fianna kinfolk and proceeded to cull all but a couple of the Garou in both tribes but the Fianna lost badly until only one young inexperienced warrior was left to lead the tribe. Since then he has attempted to force as many of his kinfolk who showed promise into becoming garou and has armed the kinfolk as heavily as possible. The locations of the caerns/spirit sites has been lost too and the Uktena have built up their forces as well.<br /> <br /> The PCs are outsiders thrust into this situation and I'd like to add some sort of spirit presence to the mix, maybe a garou revenant seeking revenge, a disturbed nature spirit, or something like that but I've only got the W20 book and there's not much in there about non-banes.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have a suitable suggestion and/or reference for some sort of spiritual adversary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T17:17:06-07:00","id":1154019,"title":"","content":"How many Caerns are you talking about in the area? Also the Fianna forcing kinfolk who show promise into becoming Garou? that's not how it works. Now I could see some kind of gang warfare in a Gangs of New York style with a pair of Caerns within the mountain range (and maybe a lost one too) with the Uktena having a couple of viable packs of Garou tending to the one and some healthy kinfolk 'gang' numbers and the Fianna maybe being down to one last small and fairly young pack holding on to their Caern and trying to bolster their own kinfolk 'gang' however they can. As for the 'disturbed spirit' if you're in a mountain range then you could totally look at it potentially being a Wendigo Spirit, or given that there have been immigrants maybe A Fenris Wolf or Wolf of the Fimbulwinter, perhaps Mountain itself is growing angered and maybe the spirit's direct involvement is WHY the third Caern is missing as the local Garou packs have proven somewhat lost in their own private little war to properly respect the Spirits and Gaia. <br /> <br /> References for spirits you want the Umbra book, Axis Mundi and if you really want to mix things up for the player characters (and its an awesome book) Rage Across the Heavens is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T18:19:25-07:00","id":1154031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1154006-looking-for-a-powerful-spirit#post1154006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ISince then he has attempted to force as many of his kinfolk who showed promise into becoming garou and has armed the kinfolk as heavily as possible. The locations of the caerns/spirit sites has been lost too and the Uktena have built up their forces as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to imply that he's making kinfolk skin-dance. Apologies, but I don't see much sense in it.<br /> <br /> First, the ritual is not common. Second, it's a level 5 ritual and he's an ahroun with no mentors, where did he even learn to cast rituals like a competent theurge? He needs a few years to teach it to the kinfolks, too. Third, it requires five garou deaths each and it feels unlikely he could have gathered enough to morph more than a single kinfolk in a garou, since they usually run around in packs. Fourth, it makes no sense for a Garou to suggest such a thing at the expense of anything but BSDs. And skindancing with BSD hides may very well bring wyrm-taint into the kinfolks. FIfth, with all the kinfolks he met no one of them reported his behaviour to some other Caern or kinfolk network?<br /> <br /> My suggestion is to change what's happening. =P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does anyone have a suitable suggestion and/or reference for some sort of spiritual adversary? </div> </div> </div>There's a spirit called Black Stag if I correctly remember, an aspect of the totem spirit Stag, patron of the Fianna tribe. The Black Stag is a spirit strongly focused on battle and vengeance against the enemies of Gaia. He will definitely attack anything with Wyrm or Weaver taint, so he's probably going to wreck every skin dancer he finds. It's not a spirit that would attack Gaian garou though, so you should specify which side of the conflict you want him for.<br /> <br /> It's mentioned in Umbra revised, and marked as WP 10, Rage 9, Gnosis 7, with Blast (fire) and Armor charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T02:01:33-07:00","id":1154075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1154006-looking-for-a-powerful-spirit?p=1154019#post1154019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the Fianna forcing kinfolk who show promise into becoming Garou? that's not how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know that, the last Fianna Garou doesn't, he thinks that 'sufficient stress' will make kinfolk turn so he's pretty much running a bunch of teens ragged by training them in the woods (vicious hand to hand combat, outrageously difficult assault courses, cross country 'pursuits', etc)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1154006-looking-for-a-powerful-spirit?p=1154031#post1154031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to imply that he's making kinfolk skin-dance.</div> </div> </div> </div>No the last Fianna isn't the skin dancer, the skin dancer moved away a long time ago, this is just what was left behind<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1154006-looking-for-a-powerful-spirit?p=1154019#post1154019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">perhaps Mountain itself is growing angered and maybe the spirit's direct involvement is WHY the third Caern is missing as the local Garou packs have proven somewhat lost in their own private little war to properly respect the Spirits and Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an excellent idea, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 10-30-2017, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T05:15:53-07:00","id":1154092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1154006-looking-for-a-powerful-spirit?p=1154075#post1154075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know that, the last Fianna Garou doesn't, he thinks that 'sufficient stress' will make kinfolk turn so he's pretty much running a bunch of teens ragged by training them in the woods (vicious hand to hand combat, outrageously difficult assault courses, cross country 'pursuits', etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! Thank you, it makes a lor more sense now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}